4. Details of the share capital, [?], guarantees, loans, [?] and other resources provided or agreed to be provided by each shareholder company;
5. The business benefits and feasibility studies considered as the basis for the decision to establish this company;
6. Whether the establishment of this company complied with the Companies Act, the PCB's principles, the public finance regulations and the corporate governance principles that state-owned companies must follow;
7. How the managing director and board members were appointed, and whether there was any conflict of interest in that;
8. Whether the policy this company follows in procuring goods and services (procurement) is as transparent as that of state-owned companies;
9. Whether this company falls within the scope of oversight of the PCB and the Auditor General;
10. Whether, as a result of establishing a company under such a [?], state assets, expenditure, debts and project matters have moved outside the system of accountability that state companies are subject to; and
11. Whether establishing an additional company under the existing three companies conflicts with the government's policy of reducing the number of companies and strengthening their management.

Furthermore, the shareholders in this newly established private company are three companies in which the government holds shares. Therefore, establishing a new private company using the capital of those companies amounts to working to change the nature of state-owned property.

Accountability in the use and management of state resources is an important responsibility placed on the People's Majlis by the Constitution. The SOE Committee has also previously looked into matters relating to the management, finances and procurement of state companies. Matters relating to the spending of state funds also fall within the remit of the Public Finance Committee.

Therefore, I respectfully request that the Speaker send this matter to the SOE Committee, and send the [?] parts relating to the spending of state funds to the Public Finance Committee for review.

For the purpose of this study, I request that the company's incorporation documents, its articles of association, shareholder agreements, board resolutions, approvals from the PCB and the Ministry of Finance, corporate plans, feasibility studies and details of how it was financed be obtained.
